WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:05.819
Hi, I'm Kristen. I'm a professor for an online Master's degree in chemistry and biochemistry.

00:00:06.279 --> 00:00:11.789
But some days. I really miss teaching undergraduates ochem, so welcome to my classroom.

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:17.279
Educapability is my effort to make organic chemistry more accessible for you.

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:23.419
OChem is a really challenging subject; we need to visualize

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:26.070
three-dimensional structures in our mind,

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:32.299
but then we need to draw those in two dimensions on paper to produce work for exams and things like that.

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:34.469
We also need to recognize

00:00:34.469 --> 00:00:39.499
electron density hot spots on one part of the molecule and how those might interact with an

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:44.329
electronically cold spot on another molecule to form a chemical bond.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:51.080
We also need to be able to show that process by drawing curved arrows that show where the electrons are moving.

00:00:52.409 --> 00:00:58.909
Organic chemistry is extremely visual so I'll use a variety of media to help convey these challenging topics

00:00:59.489 --> 00:01:01.489
We'll use handheld models,

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:04.640
computer generated models, and molecular

00:01:05.339 --> 00:01:09.228
animation so you can see where the bonds are breaking and forming. I

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:17.420
hope that through my videos you're able to gain an understanding of reactivity so you don't just need to memorize every reaction mechanism

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:20.509
which is so hard. You can actually go through and

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:27.110
be like this is my electron hot spot and my arrow has to come from there. Once you can do that and gain that ability

00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:33.169
organic chemistry can be really satisfying. It becomes like a logic puzzle, and it can actually be fun.

00:01:33.170 --> 00:01:36.830
I hope to share some of my enjoyment for organic chemistry with you.

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:39.380
Thanks for watching.

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:48.600
 

